# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 07: SETUP & GUIDED SETUP

**Primary route:** `/mctb/setup` | **Wizard:** `/mctb/setup/start` (or equivalent) | **Sections:** `/mctb/setup/...`  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-07-SETUP.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–06

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Setup (`/mctb/setup`, wizard, setup section routes, legacy `/voice/setup`).

## Core architecture (LOCKED)

**One canonical MCTB configuration.** Two presentations:

| State | Experience |
|-------|------------|
| First-time / incomplete | Guided wizard: Phone → Missed Calls → Consent → Text Back → Voicemail → Test & Activate |
| Configured / operational | Setup Overview — direct jump to any section; **no wizard** for single edits |

Wizard and standalone editors **read/write the same backend**. No separate onboarding settings.

## Setup Overview (`/mctb/setup`)

Configuration home with status rows: Name | Summary | Problem | Manage/Fix.

Canonical areas: Phone & Forwarding, Missed-call Rules, Text Back, Consent, **Recovery Controls** (spec 12 — replaces Business Hours + Follow-up Rules), Voicemail, Test & Diagnostics. Links/Exclusions/Numbers out of scope for this page-spec pass.

Lifecycle: **Start setup** / **Continue setup** (incomplete) | normal overview (active) | degraded problem + direct fix (no full wizard rerun).

## Wizard rules

- User-language progress (Phone, Consent, Text Back — not TFV/Pending/Runtime)
- Incremental save on advance; Back preserves fields; resume at incomplete step
- Readiness-based completion — not click-through
- Real forwarding verification evidence; real test checkpoints (not fake %)
- Press-1: locked system confirmation + editable conversation opener
- `existing_consent`: explicit attestation, never prechecked
- Sender readiness ≠ recipient consent
- External review (TFV/10DLC) — status surface, not trapping wizard step
- After activation: `/mctb/setup` opens overview, not Step 1

## Direct editors (post-setup)

Page title + purpose + status + form + Save. **No wizard progress.**

Local config nav (sidebar/list), not 10 horizontal tabs.

Voicemail greeting details: also see spec 05.

## Readiness model

Orthogonal facets — not one overloaded `setup_status`: Configuration, Forwarding, Sender, Consent, Operational mode, Health, Live test. "Needs attention" is derived.

## API

Audit legacy SolutionSetup vs MCTB setup APIs. Wizard + editors → **one** canonical configuration domain.

## Prohibited

Giant 12-section page as primary UX; separate wizard/real settings; force wizard for one change; provider jargon on overview; fake verified forwarding; editable Press-1 compliance message; fake test progress; restart wizard on partial failure

